---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About howmanycoin -- a free crypto conversion tool with live rates and supply explainers."
>

  <section class="mt-6 prose wide max-w-none">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">About howmanycoin</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-lg text-slate-600">
      Free crypto conversion rates, supply explainers, and educational guides -- no sign-up, no ads, no fluff.
    </p>

    <h2>What we do</h2>
    <p>
      howmanycoin provides instant crypto-to-fiat and crypto-to-crypto conversion rates.
      Type in any amount, see the result, and swap directly via 1inch or Jupiter if you want
      to execute a trade. We also publish plain-English explainers on token supply dynamics
      -- market cap, FDV, emissions schedules, and supply shocks -- so you can evaluate
      any token beyond just its price.
    </p>

    <h2>Why we built this</h2>
    <p>
      Most crypto sites are bloated with ads, exchange sign-up funnels, and promotional content.
      We wanted a clean, fast tool that does one thing well: show you the rates and explain
      the mechanics behind them. No accounts, no tracking, no paywalls.
    </p>

    <h2>What you can find here</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Converter pages</strong> -- 25+ live currency pairs with real-time rates, 24h change, and direct swap links</li>
      <li><strong>Supply explainers</strong> -- detailed breakdowns of token supply models for major cryptocurrencies</li>
      <li><strong>Guides</strong> -- plain-English explanations of market cap, FDV, token emissions, and supply dynamics</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Data sources</h2>
    <p>
      Live rates are sourced from <strong>CoinGecko</strong>, cached at the edge via Cloudflare
      Workers, and refreshed every 60 seconds. Supply data is sourced from CoinGecko and
      supplemented by official project documentation.
    </p>

    <h2>Transparency</h2>
    <p>
      Swap links on this site are affiliate links. If you use one, we may earn a commission
      at no extra cost to you. This does not affect the rates shown or the quality of our
      content. We do not accept payment for positive coverage of any project.
    </p>

    <h2>Get in touch</h2>
    <p>
      Have a suggestion, found an error, or want to collaborate? <a href="/contact/">Contact us</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
